From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: i2c: qcom-cci: resolve camera devices within the controller node

Use the CCI node scope when looking up the attached devices.

The port retains changes from these linux-piano commits:
piano: cameras through CAMSS and the TFE hardware ISP (#28) (bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>)

Co-authored-by: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>

Link: https://github.com/blu-sharky/linux-piano/commit/352508459733d3e6d349ea5581a8dd2fd8bb4180
Link: https://github.com/slwyts/Project-SunUEFI/commit/e8fcf33971263f28085dbc0dbe5039438bf76c13
---
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
index bd70c6bae5dc685435bf2ad031cf7a11ec60ab4f..d55806c89c06a4a65b0f8c3eba3b4928f65b6b36 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
@@ -520,6 +520,13 @@ static int cci_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (!cci->data)
 		return -ENOENT;
 
+	/*
+	 * cci_reset() always waits on master 0, and the interrupt handler may
+	 * complete either master, whether or not the board uses it.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < NUM_MASTERS; i++)
+		init_completion(&cci->master[i].irq_complete);
+
 	for_each_available_child_of_node_scoped(dev->of_node, child) {
 		struct cci_master *master;
 		u32 idx;
@@ -558,8 +565,6 @@ static int cci_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			else if (val == I2C_MAX_FAST_MODE_PLUS_FREQ)
 				master->mode = I2C_MODE_FAST_PLUS;
 		}
-
-		init_completion(&master->irq_complete);
 	}
 
 	/* Memory */
